From 8f773471924b183a33333757f899fe4da8c29351 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 10:19:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] storage, translation, network and media kits: fix what the
 static analysis found

- BQuery: an unquoted '%' without its closing '%' made _ParseDates() loop
  forever ("name==100%", or Tracker's Find with a '"' and a '%'), and an
  escaped quote ended the quoting.
- The text sniffer (in the registrar) read its UTF-16 buffer past the
  length it had filled: in the troff check for a file that is only a BOM or
  a "." line, and in the keyword scan for any multibyte text.
- BTranslatorRoster: every directory of a path list but the last lost its
  last character, and a missing directory added garbage to the count.
- BNetEndpoint: IsDataPending() on a closed endpoint did FD_SET(-1).
- BNetworkAddress: IPv6 prefix lengths were rounded down to whole bytes.
- BMediaFile: a file that no reader takes, a writer without a format, or
  SetTo(BUrl) leaked the BFile (or adapter) and its descriptor.
- BMediaEncoder: SetFormat() with an output format that no encoder takes
  released the encoder and then used it.
- BMediaTheme: a parameter web without groups made the default theme use a
  tab view it never created.
- BFileInterface: the formats were advanced by sizeof(media_format)
  elements at a time.
- BMediaClientNode: a buffer for an input that is gone crashed the node.
- BAdapterIO: FlushBefore() leaked the new buffer whenever it did not adopt
  it, and hid the error.

Test: HaikuArmQemu's tools/analysis-fixes/afxtest, query-lone-percent,
text-sniffer, translator-path-list, net-endpoint-closed,
ipv6-prefix-length, media-file-descriptors, media-encoder-bad-format,
media-theme-empty-web and adapter-io-flush.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0145-storage-translation-network-and-media-kits-fix-what-the-stat.patch f8b5cd93309b9ce2d3bde9b2679186ec2354a46a3dd5ec44b179cfa8ca71947a
